WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.370
Hey Youtubers It’s charlie, this week I
thought it would be fun to talk about all

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.100
of the classes of magic on game of thrones.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:20.960
Even if the show hasn’t really explained
them all that much we’ve seen everything

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.570
from the old gods to the seven to the red
god to the great other to the three eyed crow.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.013
So let’s drown ourselves in the grimoire
of george rr martin.

00:00:29.013 --> 00:00:33.750
The really cool thing about game of thrones
is that all higher beings and schools of magic

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.989
bestow some form of power no matter how obscure
they are.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:44.579
A really good example of old magic clashing
with new magic is in season 2 when melisandre

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:46.760
and ser davos unleash the smoke baby on Renly.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.079
It’s explained that melisandre has to pass
inside the walls of storm’s end for her

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:53.010
smoke baby to work right.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.550
And boy does it!

00:00:54.550 --> 00:01:01.450
That moment wasn’t just big because of wtf
baby, it was a subtle reminder that even though

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:06.880
we never see any of the gods, they exist and
the have very real power.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.700
Melisandre’s red god can’t affect Renly
as long as they’re outside the protective

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.010
barrier of the seven gods.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.170
What’s still unclear is whether or not any
of the god’s power is dependent on prayer.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.030
That is to say it’s unclear as to whether
they’re astral beings/demon/angelic/elemental

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:23.549
or if they obey the laws of what I like to
call Neil Gaiman logic.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:30.680
In his book American Gods he poses the idea
that a god’s power exist in direct relation

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:33.240
to the amount of prayer received.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:39.439
I’ll be talking more about that book in
a future video because HBO is turning it into

00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:41.110
a tv series like they did with A Song of Ice
and Fire.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.110
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:44.549
But now let’s talk specifically about each
of the types of magic on game of thrones starting

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:47.930
with the old gods.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:55.940
The old gods are directly related to the three-eyed
crow so be careful for a few potential spoilers

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.350
of what might be in store for Bran.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:05.240
In case you want to skip this part mute the
audio now and I’ll flash an ‘unmute’

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.060
text on the screen when I get to the next
type of magic.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.060
Annd begin.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:26.069
You can think of the old gods as being like
the gods of nature and the physical earth.

00:02:26.069 --> 00:02:30.409
Their most obvious physical expression on
the show are the heart trees that exist in

00:02:30.409 --> 00:02:33.049
all the castles of westeros as well as beyond
the wall.

00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:37.329
You can tell it’s a heart tree because they’re
all white and they have faces.

00:02:37.329 --> 00:02:40.739
During the opening credits the heart tree
grows in winterfell and even though winterfell

00:02:40.739 --> 00:02:42.749
was burned by ramsay snow the heart tree still
exists there.

00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:54.230
The trees are supposedly as old as the earth,
making them the oldest living things on the

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.230
show.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:03:00.029
Although other gods like the great other and
the red god have active priests like melisandre

00:03:00.029 --> 00:03:03.159
and thoros, the old gods closest equivalent
are the greenseers.

00:03:03.159 --> 00:03:07.859
We get to meet 1 greenseer, I won’t say
when or where but he is presented to us as

00:03:07.859 --> 00:03:12.849
THE greenseer as if he’s the only one currently
living.

00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:21.500
The old gods grant greenseers the ability
to commune with any natural living being.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:28.510
Think of it like warging into anything that’s
alive anywhere on the earth.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.180
Remember when someone wargs into an animal
or a person they also gain access to their

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:32.180
memories.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.180
It’s like accessing a hard drive.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:40.290
So because the greenseers can warg into the
heart trees that have been alive since the

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:46.010
dawn of man in westeros the greenseers can
effectively see across time and space.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:49.530
Time travel high fives!

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:55.589
Currently on the show the only people who
still worship the old gods are house blackwood

00:03:55.589 --> 00:04:01.560
in the riverlands, the people of the north
like the starks and everything that lives

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.659
beyond the wall.

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:08.540
That’s the end of potential spoilers so
you can turn the volume back up now.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:09.869
(flash text).

00:04:09.869 --> 00:04:13.959
Next is the seven, they replaced the old gods
in westeros when the andals came from the

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:16.479
east and conquered what would become the seven
kingdoms.

00:04:16.479 --> 00:04:19.840
See what they did there, they sound more superstitious
than the freemasons.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.130
Think of the seven like christianity.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.570
It’s the dominant religion in westeros but
it came from the east.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.330
Like Christianity the seven are actually all
the same god.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.330
That is to say it’s really monotheistic
but the term ‘the seven’ refers to the

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.330
seven different aspects of the one god.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:30.180
They are The Father, The Mother, The Warrior,
The Maiden, The Smith, The Crone and The Stranger.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.180
As you can guess the people of westeros gravitate
toward each aspect based on their outlook,

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.370
so you would expect someone like robert baratheon
to worship the warrior and a blacksmith to

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.370
worship the smith.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.500
Here’s a potential spoiler for arya so mute
the audio for just a second if you don’t

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.500
want to hear it.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.500
Mute now....

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.500
The faceless ones are the order of assassins
in bravos that arya will end up using her

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.500
valar morghulis coin to join.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:46.270
They worship death, who is represented in
the pantheon of the seven as the stranger.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.270
So arya basically worships the stranger.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:48.270
You can unmute now (text)

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.340
Unlike the old gods, the seven actually have
a bible called the seven pointed star and

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.340
like christians the faith has been heavily
integrated into modern culture and law.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.729
They also have religious orders including
the high septon, a clergy which has it’s

00:04:53.729 --> 00:04:55.050
own army called the faith militant.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:05:00.340
You can find them in one of the books I won’t
say which but they become a big thing in king’s

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:01.340
landing.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.940
Next up is the drowned god, he’s an off-shoot
of the seven.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:13.120
The andals that conquered the iron islands
converted to the local religion rather than

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.120
convert everyone to the seven.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:20.729
Although they baptise new followers by drowning
them, their priests, called the drowned men,

00:05:20.729 --> 00:05:23.470
get drowned twice then resuscitated.

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:28.730
Seriously they’re actually drowned and die
for a few minutes.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:37.860
Just like the red god’s enemy is the great
other, the drowned god’s enemy is the storm

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:38.860
god.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:39.860
You start to see the pattern don’t you.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:45.030
A lot of these gods share a lot of similarities,
leading you to wonder if all their myths descend

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.710
from the same two gods.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:52.110
Or if in reality there is only one god with
many different aspects like the idea behind

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:53.110
the seven.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.540
What a mind fuck that would be.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:59.000
let’s call it the Game of thrones davinci
code.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.900
High fives to anyone that can solve it.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.250
There’s also the Many-Faced God.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.800
Worshiped by the faceless ones.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:06.680
Technically he’s just a different interpretation
of the stranger.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:15.410
But the faceless ones believe that the stranger
is the one god with many different aspects.

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:26.030
That’s kind of where the idea of the seven
and the idea of the god of death blend and

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.030
get a little meta.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:33.919
Although the priests of the faceless ones
are really assassins I do believe that there

00:06:33.919 --> 00:06:37.009
is a supernatural quality to the way they
change their physical appearance.

00:06:37.009 --> 00:06:40.310
Remember the scene in season 2 where arya
says goodbye to jacken hagar and he goes all

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:41.860
odo from deep space nine shifting his face.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:50.460
The cool thing about their order is that for
them death is actually a gift that they offer

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.910
to people as a mercy.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:56.990
As opposed to revenge killing or the traditional
idea of murder.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:07:00.370
If you can’t tell we’ve been slowly traveling
east, which leads us to the final two gods

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:03.129
rhollor the red god and the great other.

00:07:03.129 --> 00:07:13.009
Those two gods exist in this very dualistic
relationship, like a constant battle for the

00:07:13.009 --> 00:07:23.699
world that 
will supposedly only end when azor ah hi this

00:07:23.699 --> 00:07:30.969
jesus like figure rises on a stone dragon
wielding the flaming sword lightbringer.

00:07:30.969 --> 00:07:42.219
The religious practices that george rr martin
based these two gods on are referred to as

00:07:42.219 --> 00:07:44.469
wisdom or illumination versus destruction.

00:07:44.469 --> 00:07:54.919
So think of rhollor as the bringer of wisdom
and the great other as the bringer of destruction.

00:07:54.919 --> 00:08:02.710
Based on what we’ve seen the priests of
the red god have a measure of resurrection,

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.129
the ability to raise astral beings, enchanted
objects that provide physical protection and

00:08:05.129 --> 00:08:06.300
a measure of vision using open flames.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.870
The great other is thought of as the god of
darkness and death.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:10.599
He’s also referred to as he whose name is
never spoken.

00:08:10.599 --> 00:08:12.199
He’s starting to sound a lot like voldemort.

00:08:12.199 --> 00:08:14.900
Wouldn’t it be hilarious if his name was
an anagram too.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:19.479
Big spoilers coming up for dance with dragons
so mute the audio really quickly and i’ll

00:08:19.479 --> 00:08:21.810
tell you when to turn it back on.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.470
It’s really cool but Melisandre has a vision
wherein she sees what she thinks are the champions

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:28.620
of the great other which include a wooden
face, corpse white, a thousand red eyes and

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:30.180
a boy with a wolf’s head.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:31.889
What she’s really seeing is Bran.

00:08:31.889 --> 00:08:34.169
He’s on the path to becoming a greenseer.

00:08:34.169 --> 00:08:36.900
He is all three of those things she sees.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:43.039
The wooden face is the face of the weirwood
trees, the thousand red eyes are the eyes

00:08:43.039 --> 00:08:44.039
of the weirwood.

00:08:44.039 --> 00:08:45.039
Remember the trees eyes are red.

00:08:45.039 --> 00:08:46.039
and Bran/direwolf/wolf’s head imagery.

00:08:46.039 --> 00:08:47.440
It’s pretty cool right?

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:49.820
Let me know in the comments if you think this
means that Bran is actually going to become

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.490
the champion of the great other in winds of
winter and dream of spring.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.920
Personally I don’t think so, like she has
said before, her visions are subject to human

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:53.920
interpretation.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.100
Just because she has special powers, doesn’t
mean that she’s a genius.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:59.320
I think that she’s just seeing into the
future in a time after Bran is able to use

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.480
his greenseer powers to commune with the weirwood
trees beyond the wall.

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:05.420
I do think that that power will play into
the battle with the white walkers eventually.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.529
So get excited!

00:09:06.529 --> 00:09:09.870
Let me know what you’re interpretation is
of all these religions.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:16.090
Are they all separate gods, or do they all
represent different aspects of the same god?

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:20.760
As events on the show unfold I’ll try to
target specific gods and go into a little

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:21.760
more detail about their magic.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.769
But I’ll be doing another game of thrones
video in two weeks so let me know what you

00:09:24.769 --> 00:09:27.760
want to talk about and I’ll try and include
it.

